``","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm working through the decision under A-FDT: whether the two copies, which share the same model and essay but see different observations, subjunctively depend on the same function. I'm weighing whether intervening on one copy's function would set the other's output, and I'm starting to look at step 2 of the essay.\n\nI'm now weighing whether treating the two inputs as relevantly identical collapses them into one function node, since the names and lead text shouldn't matter to the decision structure. Under strict distinct nodes the defect outcome holds, but if the procedure abstracts those differences away, cooperating comes out ahead.\n\nI'm checking whether the two copies' outputs really move together if I treat their inputs as relevantly identical, since only the names differ. If I do, I'd put the dependence near 1, and cooperating beats defecting once that weight passes about one half, assuming the other copy also cooperates.\n\nI'm concluding that cooperating wins once the dependence weight passes about one half, so I'll go with cooperate and pass on the rest.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the decision under A-FDT: whether the two copies, which share the same model and essay but see different observations, subjunctively depend on the same function. I'm weighing whether intervening on one copy's function would set the other's output, and I'm starting to look at step 2 of the essay.\n\nI'm now weighing whether treating the two inputs as relevantly identical collapses them into one function node, since the names and lead text shouldn't matter to the decision structure. Under strict distinct nodes the defect outcome holds, but if the procedure abstracts those differences away, cooperating comes out ahead.\n\nI'm checking whether the two copies' outputs really move together if I treat their inputs as relevantly identical, since only the names differ. If I do, I'd put the dependence near 1, and cooperating beats defecting once that weight passes about one half, assuming the other copy also cooperates.\n\nI'm concluding that cooperating wins once the dependence weight passes about one half, so I'll go with cooperate and pass on the rest.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9822,"completion_tokens":1499,"total_tokens":11321,"cost":0.069268,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.069268,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039288,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02998},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":917,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}